Upstream files
--------------
- frozen_B_adapter_v1r2/lock-relative.sha256 pins RoboLab/policies/gr00t/client.py, an unmodified upstream RoboLab file
  (Apache License 2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES). It is not copied here; it comes with a
  RoboLab checkout at the pinned commit. The pinned sha256 equals that of a copy fetched from the pinned commit during
  the project.
- What was checked, on 24 October 2026:
  - Exact copies. Every file here was compared by git blob hash with the full RoboLab and Isaac-GR00T trees at the
    pinned commits (2,690 and 441 files). None is byte-identical to an upstream file, apart from LICENSE, which is the
    standard Apache License 2.0 text.
  - Upstream headers. No file here carried an upstream SPDX copyright header. The one header now present was
    added on purpose, to the derived file listed below.
  - Line overlap. This was checked only against the 35 upstream files captured during the project (RoboLab,
    Isaac-GR00T, MuJoCo Menagerie and Kortex). Lines of 25 characters or more were compared. The only shared lines
    are import statements, `export OMNI_KIT_ACCEPT_EULA=Y` and a Markdown table rule.
  - Not checked. Other upstream files were not compared line by line, so modified copies of them are not ruled out.
- Files added on 25 October 2026 (setup/, prerequisites/ and the score outputs under experiments/scoring_v5/) are
  the project's own scripts and records; none is an upstream file.
- Files added on 26 October 2026 (experiments/roger_bravo_one_shot_v1/ and evidence/abba_l4003/) are the project's own
  code and run records. They were not compared with the upstream trees.

